{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Residual: a stale in-code assertion of the retracted req-0022 claim\n\nRecording so it is not lost. `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py:486-497` still carries a\ncomment asserting the duplicate-`Task` finding as FACT. With req-0022 retracted in Gerrit 1394 ps2,\nthat comment now contradicts the doc, and it sits ~10 lines above the evidence emitter (`:499-534`)\nthat produced the contradicting measurement — so the next reader gets the refuted claim and its\nrefutation from the same file.\n\n**Deliberately NOT fixed yet, and by whom:** that file is inside the blast radius of the in-flight\nDC parent-hierarchy stream ([rebar:9f26-66c2-14af-4223] / [rebar:4b9e-bcad-456a-4233]). Editing it\nnow risks a conflict for a comment-only change, and interrupting that stream to reconcile a comment\nis a bad trade. I own it and will land it once the hierarchy stream is in.\n\n**Verified independently** (not taken from a report): the recorded digest in the doc, the Dockerfile\npin in 1394 ps2, and the pin at `d394a70529` (the commit run 30951453979 ran) are all\n`sha256:04326628dc4ac36b2bfc1d0f2ebe5ba3807c1ec9cf9b18307d3c2ad7222537e9` — byte-identical. So this\nis a SAME-DIGEST contradiction and base-image drift is ruled out mechanically. My earlier framing of\nit as probable image drift was wrong.\n\nThat is the point this ticket exists for: two of the three contradicted claims were wrong about the\nimage we actually run, and neither was detectable by any check that existed. A digest gate answers\n'is this a different image', which is necessary and insufficient."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785884860917209001,"uuid":"274ca539-27df-4516-9afd-e5083ae2002b"}